course: dictionary
lesson: 14399
title: Getting ahead
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To outpace someone means to go faster than them, so you get ahead. Think of a race: if you run faster than your friend and pass them, you outpace them. You can also outpace something that is not a person, like a dog chasing you or a wave on the beach.
explain: Outpace can also be about growth. When one thing grows or improves faster than another, it outpaces it. «Our bean plant grew so fast that it outpaced the sunflower.» The bean did not run anywhere. It grew faster, so it got ahead in height.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. Who or what is fast? Who is behind? Words like «easily» tell you the gap is big: «She easily outpaced the others.» Easily means without trying hard, so she was much faster than them.
fact: Outpace means to go faster than someone or something, so you get ahead.
fact: Outpace can also mean to grow or improve faster than something else.
fact: The past form is «outpaced», and the -ing form is «outpacing»: «She is outpacing him.»
fact: «Easily outpace» means to beat someone without much effort.
fact: The start out- often means "more than" or "beyond", as in outrun and outgrow.
exercise: In the race, Mia ran so fast that she outpaced everyone else. What does outpaced mean? | Waved to the crowd | *Went faster than and got ahead of | Fell behind the others | Stopped to tie her laces
exercise: «The hare easily outpaced the tortoise.» Was the hare quicker or slower? | *Quicker | Asleep under a tree | Slower | The same speed
exercise: Jo says, «Prices outpaced wages.» What does this mean? | Wages rose faster than prices | Prices and wages stayed exactly the same | *Prices rose faster than wages | Wages were paid in coins
test: Ali wrote, «The dog chased the boy, but the boy outpaced it and reached home first.» Who got ahead? | Ali | *The boy | The dog | Nobody
test: Which word is the past form of outpace? | outpace | *outpaced | outpaces | outpacing
exam: «The new phone outpaced the old one in speed and battery life.» What does outpaced mean here? | Stayed exactly the same as the old one | Went slower than the old one | Stopped working altogether | *Improved faster than the old one, so it got ahead
